# Design request workflow

```text
Brief → Research + Prototype (one turn) → Iterate → Export to Figma
```

## Routing

| Designer signal | Skill |
| --- | --- |
| New brief: "design a…", "I need a screen for…", "continue <slug>" | `design-request` |
| "Research…", "how do other apps…", "research first" | `design-research` |
| "Prototype this", "build it", "make it clickable" | `design-prototype` |
| Changes or comments on an existing prototype | `design-iterate` |
| "Export/push/send to Figma", Figma file link after approval | `design-export-figma` (not the official `figma-generate-design`) |
| Figma Design frame link + "inspect/spec/review" | `inspect-design` |
| FigJam board link + "summarize" | `figjam-summary` |

## Request folder

```text
prototypes/<slug>/
├── research.md       # sources and recommended starter/states
├── board.html        # visual research board: screenshots by theme, starter and states
├── references/       # screenshots cited on the board
├── index.html        # current prototype
├── notes.md          # version, states table, changelog, Figma export record
├── feedback.md       # ID · date · source · feedback · priority · status · version
└── history/<version>.html
```

A temporary `prototypes/<slug>/.capture/` exists only during export and is
deleted afterwards.

## Checkpoints

- **Fast path (default):** one checkpoint after the prototype.
- **Research first (opt-in):** an extra checkpoint after `research.md` and
  `board.html`.
- Every research run, compact or full, writes `board.html`; missing
  screenshots are marked on their cards, never a reason to skip the board.
- Every phase ends with three to five numbered options; the designer replies
  with a digit or free text.

## Preview and export

- Preview (`board.html` and `index.html`): Canvas first; a localhost server
  rooted at the request folder is the fallback.
- Export: always served from localhost, from the `.capture/` copy, one
  390×844 frame per `?state=<id>`, into the Figma file the designer links for
  that export. Never guess a destination.

## Figma preflight

Before any Figma tool call, confirm the official Figma plugin skills and
remote tools are present. If missing, stop that step and tell the designer to
run `/add-plugin figma`, reload Cursor, and retry. On an auth error, stop and
point to **Customize → Plugins → Figma → Connect/Authenticate** (OAuth). Never
request a PAT or add a Bearer header.
